    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive attack, both benefiting from significant platoon advantages against right-handed pitching that pushed their efficiency scores to 81.00 and 73.66, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** occupies the lead-off spot against Cavalli, where his dynamic platoon split (+14%) and leadoff leverage (+10%) create the highest ceiling in our lineup. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** is a high-value play at 63.68; his elite .402 xwOBA against Taillon makes him a premium start despite the park factors, as his ability to consistently reach base provides a stable floor for our daily Roto targets.\n\nOur primary bench dilemma centered on **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 44.15 score, narrowly missing the cut behind the more efficient mid-tier infielders. While **Coby Mayo** possesses intriguing power upside, the combination of his lower position in the batting order (-6%) and the slight negative platoon adjustment against Cavalli relegated him to a depth role today. We remain cautious regarding **Jackson Merrill**, whose 52.77 score is dampened by a clash with Gilbert, an elite arm (2.98 xERA) who mandates a lower expectation for output. We are also monitoring the status of **Kyle Tucker** and **Jordan Westburg**, who remain sidelined; their absence continues to stress our depth, making every marginal start from players like **Liam Hicks** (54.28) and **Drake Baldwin** (54.82) critical to maintaining our pace in the 5x5 standings.",
